-- title:
--   Henselian lift of a k-point off the crossings
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $p$ is a prime, $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5\le M$ (`hM`) and $p\nmid M$ (`hpM`), $L$ a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity (`hζ`). The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and `hK` requires $K=\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,L\,(\mathrm{x1FunctionField}\,(Mp))$, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise embedding [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), of the $q$-expansion realisation $\mathrm{x1FunctionField}(Mp)\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. The ring $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field; `hAp` puts $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and `hζA` requires $\zeta$ to lie in the image of $A$; $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Finally $j\in K$ has Laurent series $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,L\,(\mathrm{jq})$ (`hj`), the $q$-expansion of the modular function $j$, and $j\neq 0$. Write $X=\mathrm{TwoChartModel}\,A\,K\,j$ and $f=\mathrm{modelTo}\,A\,K\,j\colon X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$ for the two-chart model, glued from the finite and infinite chart algebras; $f$ is assumed proper.
--
--   *Special fibre.* $k$ is an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$. Two schemes $C_1,C_2$ are given, proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral over $\operatorname{Spec}k$ via $c_1,c_2$, together with closed immersions $i_1,i_2$ of $C_1,C_2$ into the geometric special fibre $X_k:=X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}A}\operatorname{Spec}k$ commuting with the projections to $\operatorname{Spec}k$. The hypothesis `hcover` states that every point of $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$; `hred` that the fibre product $C_1\times_{X_k}C_2$ is reduced; and `hn`, `hn0` that its underlying set has cardinality $n>0$.
--
--   *Sections.* $\varepsilon$ is a section of $f$ over $\operatorname{Spec}A$, $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2$ are sections of $c_1,c_2$, and `hε₁` requires $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ to be the base change $\mathrm{sectionBaseChange}\,k\,\varepsilon$ of $\varepsilon$.
--
--   *Relative Picard data.* $D$ is a `RelativePic0Designation` for $f$: a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec}A$ and a zero section. The hypothesis `hrep` asserts that $D$ represents the relative sub-Picard functor cut out by the fibrewise algebraically trivial condition $\mathrm{algEquivZeroCut}\,f\,\varepsilon$: there is a rigidified Poincaré bundle on the curve pulled back to $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ satisfying that condition, every rigidified line bundle satisfying it over a base $t$ is induced by a unique morphism to $D.\mathrm{toBase}$, and the pullback along the zero section is trivial. Further, $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is smooth (`hsm`) and separated (`hsep`). The hypothesis `hreps` is the corresponding representability statement over $k$ for $X_k$, the section $\mathrm{sectionBaseChange}\,k\,\varepsilon$ and $D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k$, and `hPk` asserts that its Poincaré bundle is isomorphic to the base change to $k$ (via `BaseChange.ofR`) of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some` along the first projection of $D.\mathrm{toBase}\times_{\operatorname{Spec}A}\operatorname{Spec}k$. Likewise $D_1,D_2$ are designations for $c_1,c_2$ with representability hypotheses `hrep₁`, `hrep₂`. A morphism $\nu_2$ of $k$-schemes from $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k).\mathrm{toBase}$ to $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$ is given, and `hν₂` requires, for every $k$-scheme $t\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ and every $T$-point $a$ of $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k).\mathrm{toBase}$, an isomorphism between the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₂.some` along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ and the rigidification along $\mathrm{rigSection}\,c_2\,t\,\varepsilon_2$ of the pullback along $\mathrm{curveChange}\,i_2$ of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hreps` along $a$; thus $\nu_2$ is the map induced by restricting line bundles along $i_2$.
--
--   *Geometric generic fibre.* $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb{Q}$ is an $A$-algebra and an $L$-algebra compatibly. $M_\eta$ is a `CurveModel` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp)=\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,(\mathrm{x1FunctionField}(Mp))$, that is, an integral scheme, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, whose function field is identified with that field, whose closed points are in bijection with the places of the field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with the prescribed stalk-range property, and every finite set of whose points lies in an affine open. The morphism $e_\eta\colon M_\eta.C\to X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}A}\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is an isomorphism whose composite with the second projection is $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ (`heη`). The instance `Mη_chart_nonempty` requires the preimage in $M_\eta.C$, under $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection, of the open image of the finite chart $\mathrm{ιFin}\,A\,K\,j$ to be nonempty; `hMηpin` requires that for every $a$ in the finite chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ the element of $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp)$ obtained by transporting, through $M_\eta.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, the germ at the generic point of the pullback of $a$ to that open set has Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ equal to the image under $\mathrm{coeffMap}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,L\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ of the Laurent series of $a$; so $e_\eta$ matches $q$-expansions. The hypothesis `hgal` is Galois equivariance: for every $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism $g$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ fixing the image of $L$ pointwise and every two $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x,x'$ of $M_\eta.C$ (sections of $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$), if $x'$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by the same composite for $x$, then $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x'$ is the translate of $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x$ by $\mathrm{arithmeticGalois}\,(\mathrm{x1FunctionField}(Mp))\,g$.
--
--   *Group-theoretic special fibre.* $G$ is a `NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`: abelian groups $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$, a subgroup $G.\mathrm{torus}\le G.J0s$, and a surjective homomorphism $G.\mathrm{proj}\colon G.J0s\to G.JI\times G.JE$ with kernel $G.\mathrm{torus}$. Bijections `pts`, `ptsI`, `ptsE` identify $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$ with the $k$-points of $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k).\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_1.\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$ respectively; `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` require that the Poincaré pullback along the image of a sum be isomorphic to the tensor product of the pullbacks along the images of the summands; `hproj` requires, for each $x\in G.J0s$, that $\mathrm{ptsI}$ of the first component of $G.\mathrm{proj}\,x$ be $\mathrm{pts}\,x$ followed by the morphism $\mathrm{RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom}\,i_1$ and that $\mathrm{ptsE}$ of the second component be $\mathrm{pts}\,x$ followed by $\nu_2$.
--
--   *Generic points and Hecke action.* A bijection `gpts` identifies $\mathrm{JOne}(Mp)=\mathrm{Pic}^0\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,(\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp))$ with the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}A$, additively for the relative group law supplied by `hrep.some` (`hgadd`). A map $\varphi$ assigns to each element $t$ of $\mathrm{HeckeAlgOne}$ an endomorphism of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}A$; `hφmul` requires each $\varphi\,t$ to respect the relative group law on points over every base, and `hφpts`, for the Hecke module structure $\mathrm{heckeModuleOneBar}(Mp)$ on $\mathrm{JOne}(Mp)$, requires $\mathrm{gpts}(t\cdot x)$ to be $\mathrm{gpts}\,x$ followed by $\varphi\,t$.
--
--   *Abel–Jacobi data over $L$.* `hDL` is the representability statement over $L$ for the base change of $f$ to $L$, the section $\mathrm{sectionBaseChange}\,L\,\varepsilon$ and $D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,L$, with `hPL` the corresponding base-change compatibility of Poincaré bundles. The morphism $\mathrm{ajL}$ goes from the generic fibre curve over $L$ to $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,L).\mathrm{toBase}$, sends the base-changed section to the zero section (`hajLε`), and satisfies `hajL`: for every field $K'$, every $t\colon\operatorname{Spec}K'\to\operatorname{Spec}L$ and every $t$-point $x$ of the curve, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` along $x$ followed by $\mathrm{ajL}$ is isomorphic to the tensor product of the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of the point $x$ with the ideal module of that of $t$ followed by the section, i.e. $\mathrm{ajL}$ is $x\mapsto[x]-[\varepsilon]$. The morphism $\mathrm{kL}$ from the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-fibre to the $L$-fibre of $f$ is the base-change morphism, as recorded by `hkL₁` and `hkL₂`. The morphism $\mathrm{ajbar}\colon M_\eta.C\to D.P$ is required by `hajbar` to be $e_\eta$ followed by $\mathrm{kL}$, $\mathrm{ajL}$ and the first projection of $D.\mathrm{toBase}\times_{\operatorname{Spec}A}\operatorname{Spec}L$, and `hajbar_over` states that it lies over $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}A$-structure map of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\bar\varepsilon$ of $M_\eta.C$ is the point coming from $\varepsilon$ (`hεbar`) and is sent by $\mathrm{ajbar}$ to the zero section (`hεbar_aj`). The hypothesis `hpts_aj` requires: for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x,s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ coming from $\varepsilon$ in the above sense, there is a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ on $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp)$ equal to $[\,M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,x\,]-[\,M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,s\,]$ with $\mathrm{gpts}(\mathrm{Pic0.mk}\,D_v)$ equal to $x$ followed by $\mathrm{ajbar}$.
--
--   *Igusa data on the first component.* $w$ is an `IntegralWeightOneForm k M`: a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ with an integral $q$-expansion power series whose reduction over $k$ is nonzero. $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$ is a curve model over $k$ of the Igusa function field $\mathrm{igusaFunctionFieldX1C}\,k\,M\,w$, and $e_1\colon \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C\cong C_1$ is an isomorphism over $\operatorname{Spec}k$ (`he₁`). The instance `hne₁` requires the preimage in $\mathrm{Mdl}_1.C$ of the finite chart open, along $e_1$ followed by $i_1$ and the first projection, to be nonempty. The hypothesis `hgauss₁` requires, for every $a$ in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ and all power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction over $k$: if the Laurent series of $a$ over $L$ times that of $y$ equals that of $x$, then the element of $\mathrm{igusaFunctionFieldX1C}\,k\,M\,w$ obtained from $a$ by the germ-and-$\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ construction on $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$ has Laurent series over $k$ equal to the reduction of $x$ divided by the reduction of $y$. An isomorphism of groups $\theta_1\colon G.JI\cong\mathrm{Pic}^0\,k\,(\mathrm{igusaFunctionFieldX1C}\,k\,M\,w)$ is given, subject to `hθpin₁`: for $g\in G.JI$ and a $k$-point $x$ of $c_1$, if the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₁.some` along $\mathrm{ptsI}\,g$ is isomorphic to the line bundle of the divisor of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of $\varepsilon_1$, then there is a degree-zero divisor $D_v=[\,\mathrm{Mdl}_1.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ of $x\,]-[\,\mathrm{Mdl}_1.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ of $\varepsilon_1\,]$ with $\theta_1\,g=\mathrm{Pic0.mk}\,D_v$. Lastly $\mathrm{frobIg}$ is an element of $\mathrm{SemilinearAut}\,k\,(\mathrm{igusaFunctionFieldX1C}\,k\,M\,w)$, that is, a pair of ring automorphisms of the field and of $k$ compatible with the structure map, and `hfrobIg` requires every Laurent coefficient of $\mathrm{frobIg}\cdot x$ to be the $p$-th power of the corresponding coefficient of $x$.
--
--   *An abelian subscheme.* $\mathcal{A}$ is a scheme with a morphism $a$ to $\operatorname{Spec}A$ and a morphism $\iota$ to $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $a$, which is a closed immersion (`h𝒜cl`); $a$ is proper (`h𝒜pr`) and smooth (`h𝒜sm`), and all geometric fibres of $a$ are connected (`h𝒜conn`). The hypothesis `h𝒜grp` states that for every base $s\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}A$ the $T$-points of $\mathcal{A}$, pushed forward by $\iota$, contain the identity of the relative group law of `hrep.some` and are closed under its multiplication and inversion; `h𝒜gen` states that an element $x$ of $\mathrm{JOne}(Mp)$ lies in $\mathrm{normFreePartAt}(Mp)\,p$ if and only if the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\mathrm{gpts}\,x$ factors through $\iota$; and `h𝒜hecke` states that $\mathcal{A}$ is stable under each $\varphi\,t$ on points over every base.
--
--   *The valuation ring.* $\mathrm{Pl}$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $\mathrm{Pl}$ (`hPl`), $\rho\colon A\to\mathrm{Pl}$ a ring homomorphism compatible with the structure map $A\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hρ`), $O$ a subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ contained in $\mathrm{Pl}$ (`hO`) with a compatible homomorphism $\rho_O\colon A\to O$ (`hρO`), and $\pi_k\colon\mathrm{Pl}\to k$ a surjective ring homomorphism (`hπk`) with $\pi_k\circ\rho$ the structure map $A\to k$ (`hAlgk`).
--
--   *Conclusion.* For every $k$-point $c$ of $C_1$, that is, every section of $c_1$ over the identity of $\operatorname{Spec}k$, such that for every point $t$ of $\operatorname{Spec}k$ the image $c.\mathrm{base}\,t$ does not lie in the image of the topological map underlying $\mathrm{pullback.fst}\,i_1\,i_2$ (so $c$ avoids the crossing locus $C_1\times_{X_k}C_2$), there exist a morphism $\xi\colon\operatorname{Spec}\mathrm{Pl}\to X$ whose composite with $f$ is $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho)$, and a place $P$ of $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that both of the following hold. First, $c$ followed by $i_1$ and the first projection $X_k\to X$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\pi_k)$ followed by $\xi$; that is, $\xi$ reduces to $c$. Second, $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $\mathrm{Pl}\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $\xi$ equals the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}^{-1}(P)$ of $M_\eta.C$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection $X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}A}\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to X$; that is, the generic fibre of $\xi$ is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $X$ attached to the place $P$.
--
--   This is the Henselian lifting step in the Raynaud-dictionary analysis of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring: a $k$-point of the smooth component $C_1$ lying off the crossings with $C_2$ is shown to be the reduction of a $\mathrm{Pl}$-valued point of the model whose generic fibre is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of a place of the geometric function field. It is used in the companion statement that identifies, for such a point, the associated degree-zero divisor class and its images under the two projections of the special-fibre group.
